{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1542055-best-conspirancy-or-plot-twist-in-vampire-the-masquerade","id":1542055,"title":"Best Conspirancy or Plot Twist in Vampire the Masquerade","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-13T09:22:55-07:00","id":1542055,"title":"Best Conspirancy or Plot Twist in Vampire the Masquerade","content":"What was the biggest conspiracy or plot twist you witnessed in a Vampire the Masquerade game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T09:35:14-07:00","id":1542058,"title":"","content":"1. <b>Smiling Jack</b>'s fake Antediluvian in Bloodlines is still pretty damn classic because the players never would have suspected it, let alone the Kindred.<br /> <br /> 2. <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/380147/the-murder-of-modius\" target=\"_blank\">I adapted my favorite adventure in Gary to the RPGNow Module, <i>The Murder of Modius</i></a>, that basically had the death of <b>Modius</b> be something that no Kindred could solve because everyone was suspecting one of the major power brokers when it was actually the Anarch Herald (<b>Arthur</b>) and Camarilla Sheriff (<b>Eric Sharpe</b>) doing it without their bosses' knowledge (just because Modius had pissed them off so much).<br /> <br /> The only reason there's a chance of solving it ends up being that Modius' FRIGGING GHOST comes back to annoy people (and can't identify his killers because he never bothered to learn the new Kindred of his city's identities and assumes Juggler is behind it against all evidence).<br /> <br /> We also find out that <b>Lucian</b> set up most of this as a distraction from the fact he was entering torpor to stop himself from being Beckoned. This, ironically, leading to Modius intending to diablerize him even though he no longer has a body. Good game.<br /> <br /> The players ended up just making everything worse and more complicated with Modius' &quot;Help.&quot; It was glorious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-13-2024, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T09:56:01-07:00","id":1542063,"title":"","content":"In my longest running Dark Ages chronicle for the modern nights, my players' coterie were truly shocked when they finally discovered that Capadocius, Saulot, and Tzimisce caused the origin of the Baali and that Saulot tried to eliminate the accidental Embrace of the Baali by decreeing the Baali Wars. The corrupted Tzimisce made a pact with Kupala, attracting the attention of Samiel, who hunted him down and destroyed his physical form before he himself died. The coterie was also tormented by the fact that Saulot let his clan die while he himself risked everything by trying to control the Tremere to use them as a tool in the Jyhad to attack Tzimisce and their childer. They witnessed and investigated the founders to the point of discovering that Capadocius' rivals let the Giovanni eliminate the clan to pay for the ancient crimes of having helped to conceive the Baali in the first place. Finally, they witnessed the emergence of the Valderie while the Tzimisce himself manipulated Lugoj, Velya and Vykos to form a blood rite capable of contaminating an entire sect (Sabath) and leaving it under the influence of the Tzimisce until the end of time for the former to claim the Sabath as a tool of war or a herd of vampiric blood. In the final nights with the emergence of Ur Shulgi, they traveled the world in search of information about the Assamite Methuselah, until they stumbled upon the truth, that Hakim embraced him and let him lead the Baali during the fall of the Second City so that the Baali would later be defeated. In the end, discovering that Capadocius, Saulot, Tzimisce and Ur Shulgi were responsible for the emergence of the Baali was the greatest conspiracy of my chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T11:44:09-07:00","id":1542328,"title":"","content":"The biggest plot twist for my Malkavian would be learning that Mithras doesn't want my character dusted as a reminder of Valerius time as Prince of London who decided to spare my character unauthorized embrace by his sire and put her to put final death and had my guy by mentored by my grandsire and great grandsire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T17:27:08-07:00","id":1542345,"title":"","content":"When I ran Transylvania Chronicles, the three relevant PC's to the absolute shitshow I'm about to describe were a Ventrue (Jurgen's childe), Cappadocian (Giovanni), and a Setite. They got through the first story and settled in Kronstadt (Brasov), which due to the Ventrue being Jurgen's childe was quickly converted into a Black Cross stronghold.<br /> <br /> Naturally this caused a <i>little</i> bit of a problem with the Tzimisce, but &quot;luckily&quot; the Giovanni got along rather well with Vykos when they met. So well in fact, the Giovanni started feeding Vykos information and gifted him Sherazina -- once he found out she was a surviving Basarab scion (he found the genealogy scrolls in the castle), and that Vykos was on the lookout for those. Meanwhile, the Ventrue met and managed to coexist with Ilias -- she didn't take kindly to the Black Cross forcefully converting the locals to Christianity, and worked with Ilias to sneak pagans out of the domain.<br /> <br /> Also, the Setite being a Setite discovered a black market, and drug and slave route, going through Bran Pass. He did some digging, and discovered this was part of some resource network (he didn't know at the time it was Geza Arpad's, to keep Bulscu blitzed off his tits). His original job was to go to Transylvania, meet up with a lector-priest, and assist him...the <i>lector-priest's</i> job was to find and undermine this trade route to convert Geza and Bulscu to the Road of Typhon. Except along the way he ate a Malkavian and started getting Kupala visions, which caused him to go rogue, but blunder into the trade route (and try to exploit it for personal gain).<br /> <br /> That slave route also happened to pass through Vykos' domains in Wallachia. The Giovanni and Ventrue were the ones with trade influence and resources, so he made a deal with them to keep the black market route going under his watchful eye (and interference).<br /> <br /> Naturally, the Ventrue told Jurgen and the Giovanni told Vykos. Completely independently of one another, without anyone else's knowledge. Both Jurgen and Vykos were able to figure out <i>exactly</i> what was up, and of course they didn't tell the PC's. Jurgen and Vykos wanted Bulscu out of the picture -- Jurgen as a blow against the Magyar ventrue, Vykos because Ventrue altogether.<br /> <br /> In fact, Jurgen didn't just greenlight the Setite's plan, he gave them instructions on exactly how to do it better and dominated everyone to think it was <i>their</i> idea all along. When they approached Vykos, he was <i>more</i> than happy to accommodate -- and even interceded on their behalf with Rustovich, when he came calling with a giant fucking Tzimisce army to murder them all. And he was feeding information to Nova Arpad at the same time to foster Ventrue infighting, because why the fuck not.<br /> <br /> So with the coterie acting as their own catspaw to fuck over the Magyar Ventrue on Jurgen's behalf, and Vykos playing 4D chessmaster to elevate his own standing with no one but the Giovanni being the wiser, eventually it all blows up in the PC's faces when Bulscu parties himself into torpor:<br /> <br /> - Nova tips Hardestadt off to the entire thing once she's had enough with the coterie's shit. Jurgen is dominated to literally fall on his own sword, and the Ventrue PC is called to Magdeburg to be held to account.<br /> <br /> - The Setite just gets <i>screwed</i>. The entire trade route gets uncovered by the Inquisition and shut down, and without any sort of Setite support in Transylvania, ends up with his ass hanging in the breeze and on the Ventrue Shit List.<br /> <br /> - The Giovanni makes off like a bandit. Vykos slips him word the hammer is about to come down, so he steals everything valuable he can fit in his trade caravan that isn't nailed down including <i>most</i> of the coterie's collected occult information, and flees Transylvania back to Venice.<br /> <br /> - The rest of the coterie is completely innocent in all this, but thinks they're involved because Jurgen dominated them. Except the Lasombra PC, whose domination failed. Regardless they're all implicated by association, and get to eat one giant turd sandwich together in resources, influence, domain, and status loss.<br /> <br /> But luckily, one vampire takes pity on them, and is <i>oh so happy</i> to offer long-time comrades and allies sanctuary and hospitality from the dual ravages of the Inquisition and one <i>very</i> pissed-off Ventrue clan. That vampire being Vykos, who single-handedly engineered their rise and downfall for personal gain, because of course he did. Which by implication leaves them at the mercy of Rustovich, who takes great pleasure in one-time enemies humiliated and made vassals to the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> Only for the new status quo to be blown wide open when Bulscu rises from torpor, in the middle of the Anarch Revolt...cleansed of all his past corruption, and with new purpose in unlife by way of his high rating in the Path of Chivalry. Yup, they fucked Bulscu over so hard by accident they caused a vampiric dark ages stack overflow, and turned him into a <i>good guy</i>.<br /> <br /> At the point I had to end the chronicle (fuck you Covid), Bulscu called in his favors, made it known in no uncertain terms he owns their asses because he's the only thing standing in between them and the fury of the nascent Camarilla, and that the coterie <i>will</i> help defend Christendom against the Ottomans regardless of past alliances, rivalries, grievances, and conflicts. Which would have put them <i>right</i> back where they were at the start of the whole shitshow: split loyalties, but this time around with conflicting and irreconcilable oaths to both Ventrue and Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> It's a shame the chronicle had to end, because that would have been the perfect segue into the Dracula part of the chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}